{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/497599-refinements-for-a-would-be-god","id":497599,"title":"Refinements for a would be god?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-30T10:19:57-07:00","id":497599,"title":"Refinements for a would be god?","content":"I'm planning a game where the central villain is a Promethean (osiris) and I want them to face them in three acts. First as Innocents, then add mortals then as supernatural beings. <br /> <br /> I'm trying to convey the villain trying to become his name sake, a god (rather than a puny mortal) . And I thought a good, first broad stroke wood be to work out his refinements. But I'm struggling to work out what would be appropriate... <br /> <br /> My nominations are Copper, followed by Tin, followed by Centimanti ... But the last one is almost too focused on being a monster and not a god. Also, while the first two focus on his general outlook, I envisioned the character as being far more manipulative than physically powerful. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T10:54:58-07:00","id":497634,"title":"","content":"I think you're really looking at a Hundred-Handed here. The &quot;proper&quot; refinements are roads towards humanity, not away from it; a Centimanus embraces inhumanity rather than progressing from it. There is a certain level to which the Centimani learn not to fear the fearsome and shocking, but I see nothing contradictory in a Centimanus considering its inhuman state to be exalted and superior.<br /> <br /> More to the point, though, what is the difference between a monster and a god? The World of Darkness frequently blurs that line; it's scattered across with implications that gods of myth may have been monsters of a sort, and conversely, that past monsters may have been gods. Even the religious sense of the word &quot;awe&quot; still used in contemporary worship is a sort of holy dread, interweaving feelings of admiration and terror; multiple times, the first words angels speak to men and women in the Bible have to be &quot;don't be afraid of me.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:54:50-07:00","id":497702,"title":"","content":"I've long felt that Centimanus should be split into three refinements; one of which would be for would be gods and anyone else who wants to be superior to humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T12:17:48-07:00","id":497716,"title":"","content":"It might be interesting to have him progress with them. When they first meet him, he's Iron and working on perfecting his physical form. At the next stage, he's moved on to Mercury and is refining his magical abilities. When he appears for the last time, he's completed his fall due to ignoring the Pilgrimage and is a Centimanus (and probably convinced he's achieved his goal). This gives him a story to parallel their own and lets his capabilities change over time so they can continue to be surprised by him at each new encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T12:23:02-07:00","id":497719,"title":"","content":"I've toyed (briefly) with the notion of scrapping the Centimani as a stand-alone \u201cRefinement\u201d and replacing it with a set of Corruptions that riff off of the Refinements, each taking the principles of one Refinement and twisting its goals into something Centimanus-like. System-wise, a Corruption would feature one of the root Refinement\u2019s Transmutations alongside the Pandoran Transmutations. As such, I'd aim for there to be one Corruption for every set of Transmutations in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T12:37:45-07:00","id":497734,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback it's very helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:48:10-07:00","id":499913,"title":"","content":"Argentum is also a refinement to consider- Osiris could certainly see vampires, werewolves, mages, demons, changelings, and sin-eaters as demigods, so what better way to become a god then to understand the remnants of the divine still in the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T04:03:24-07:00","id":500130,"title":"","content":"I've also heard it mentioned that Centimani isn't actually a single refinement, but rather a phylosophical lense with which to view the rest of the refinements. In this sense, he could be a Centimani-Argentum, a Centimani-Ferrum or a Centimani-Mercurius. I think its mentioned in Pandroas Book somewhere, but its been forever since I read it and I never really found the Centimani to be very interesting, honestly.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, make your own refinement. If Centimani seems too &quot;I wanna be the boogieman, Blarglbargh!&quot; then just make a new refinement thats more transhumanistic and less monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T05:26:22-07:00","id":500201,"title":"","content":"That was a fan hack, all we know about centimani in second edition is that the centimani aren't really a refinement anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T11:21:18-07:00","id":527899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/497599-refinements-for-a-would-be-god?p=497702#post497702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've long felt that Centimanus should be split into three refinements; one of which would be for would be gods and anyone else who wants to be superior to humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if the Devs have used Platinum yet. If not, I could see using a substance that's rarer, more valuable, and &quot;Nobler&quot; than Gold as a metaphor for Transhumanism.<br /> <br /> Gold was called a &quot;Noble&quot; metal for it's &quot;incorruptibility&quot;, I.E. it's resistance to rust, corrosion, or other forms of chemical change; Platinum is even less reactive. Think of it as the pursuit not necessarily of a change like the New Dawn, but of attaining a state in which one no longer NEEDS to change: becoming an everlasting, perfected being, what Dr. Frankenstein had in mind when he began his experiments. Golden Rule/S.T.'s discretion whether or not such a thing is possible...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:06:49-07:00","id":528429,"title":"","content":"&quot;A god is just a monster you kneel to&quot;-Fall of Gods<br /> <br /> Dunno if that helps in anyways, but it's relevant enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}